## Authorization Model

This feature follows the platform convention:

```text
Entra app role value = platform permission
```

Examples:

```text
[[ names.feature_key ]].view
[[ names.feature_key ]].create
[[ names.feature_key ]].edit
[[ names.feature_key ]].manage
platform.admin
```

The backend does not use local role-permission mappings.

---

## Local Authorization Testing

Local mock mode:

```env
AUTH_MODE=mock
AUTH_DEFAULT_DEV_ROLES_RAW=[[ names.feature_key ]].view
AUTH_DEBUG_HEADERS_ENABLED=true
```

Test allowed access:

```bash
curl \
  -H "X-Debug-Roles: [[ names.feature_key ]].view" \
  http://localhost:<backend-port>[[ names.api_base_path ]]/items
```

Expected:

```text
200 OK
```

Test denied access:

```bash
curl \
  -H "X-Debug-Roles: other.view" \
  http://localhost:<backend-port>[[ names.api_base_path ]]/items
```

Expected:

```text
403 Forbidden
```

Test admin access:

```bash
curl \
  -H "X-Debug-Roles: platform.admin" \
  http://localhost:<backend-port>[[ names.api_base_path ]]/items
```

Expected:

```text
200 OK
```

---

## Production Authorization

Production mode:

```env
APP_ENVIRONMENT=production
AUTH_MODE=entra
AUTH_DEBUG_HEADERS_ENABLED=false
```

Required Entra token behavior:

```json
{
  "roles": [
    "[[ names.feature_key ]].view"
  ]
}
```

Debug headers are rejected in production.

